1
00:00:00,111 --> 00:00:04,213
Have you ever seen a pillar that a
piece of cloth can slide right under?

2
00:00:04,774 --> 00:00:07,315
They say an Englishman once shook it,

3
00:00:07,756 --> 00:00:09,697
and the whole temple began to shake.

4
00:00:10,518 --> 00:00:12,859
This is Lepakshi, Andhra Pradesh.

5
00:00:13,379 --> 00:00:16,461
The Veerabhadra Temple,
about five hundred years old,

6
00:00:16,581 --> 00:00:18,362
from the Vijayanagara Empire.

7
00:00:19,003 --> 00:00:22,746
Here sits Veerabhadra, the
fierce form of Lord Shiva.

8
00:00:22,766 --> 00:00:25,049
And this whole temple is like a story

9
00:00:25,329 --> 00:00:28,933
written in stone. They say
it was built by Virupanna,

10
00:00:28,953 --> 00:00:32,337
the treasurer of King Achyuta Raya.

11
00:00:32,357 --> 00:00:34,179
There are seventy pillars here,

12
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:36,422
and one of them hangs in the air.

13
00:00:37,363 --> 00:00:39,524
Sounds like a lie, doesn't it?

14
00:00:40,104 --> 00:00:41,965
But even today, people pass

15
00:00:42,345 --> 00:00:45,266
a cloth underneath to
check. And the truth is,

16
00:00:45,846 --> 00:00:48,607
there is only a thin
gap under the pillar,

17
00:00:49,187 --> 00:00:51,488
just enough for a
cloth to slip through.

18
00:00:51,508 --> 00:00:53,909
Now, hear the story behind the name.

19
00:00:54,169 --> 00:00:58,110
In the Ramayana, when wounded
Jatayu fell, Rama said,

20
00:00:58,330 --> 00:01:00,371
Le pakshi, rise, bird.

21
00:01:02,152 --> 00:01:03,913
That is how this place got its name.

22
00:01:03,933 --> 00:01:07,935
Lepakshi. The real question is,

23
00:01:08,335 --> 00:01:10,076
why does this pillar hang?

24
00:01:10,777 --> 00:01:12,878
Was it left that way on purpose,

25
00:01:13,378 --> 00:01:14,499
or by mistake?

26
00:01:14,999 --> 00:01:15,499
Wait.

27
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:17,580
The story is not over.

28
00:01:18,141 --> 00:01:21,623
And at the end, I will tell you
the full cost of getting here.

29
00:01:22,443 --> 00:01:24,304
They say an Englishman thought,

30
00:01:24,705 --> 00:01:25,945
it must be a trick.

31
00:01:26,406 --> 00:01:29,147
He pushed the pillar, and
the whole ceiling shook.

32
00:01:30,682 --> 00:01:31,902
The pillar shifted,

33
00:01:32,203 --> 00:01:33,403
and the work stopped.

34
00:01:33,823 --> 00:01:35,604
Is the story true or not?

35
00:01:36,504 --> 00:01:37,404
No one knows.

36
00:01:37,864 --> 00:01:39,745
But the pillar is still there today.

37
00:01:39,785 --> 00:01:45,447
Ahead is the Nritya Mandapa, with gods,
sages and musicians on its pillars,

38
00:01:45,647 --> 00:01:46,987
all dancing in stone.

39
00:01:47,708 --> 00:01:48,208
Now,

40
00:01:48,788 --> 00:01:51,569
look up. On the ceiling
are colourful paintings,

41
00:01:51,649 --> 00:01:53,610
still alive after five hundred years.

42
00:01:54,730 --> 00:01:57,551
They were made with colours
from plants and minerals,

43
00:01:57,951 --> 00:02:00,252
among the finest
Vijayanagara paintings.

44
00:02:02,890 --> 00:02:06,380
Nearby is an unfinished
Kalyana Mandapa.

45
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:10,150
Work on a carved pillar
suddenly stopped.

46
00:02:10,170 --> 00:02:14,473
A folk tale says the king punished
Virupanna for exactly this.

47
00:02:15,173 --> 00:02:16,794
How much of it is true?

48
00:02:17,275 --> 00:02:18,275
No one knows,

49
00:02:18,636 --> 00:02:20,377
but the story lives on.

50
00:02:21,117 --> 00:02:25,300
About half a kilometre from
the temple sits a giant Nandi,

51
00:02:25,820 --> 00:02:27,641
carved from a single stone,

52
00:02:28,142 --> 00:02:30,303
one of the biggest Nandis in India.

53
00:02:30,683 --> 00:02:34,986
They say Nandi's face looks
straight at the temple's Nagalinga.

54
00:02:35,306 --> 00:02:39,109
And the Nagalinga is a Shivalinga
under the hood of a giant serpent,

55
00:02:39,609 --> 00:02:41,612
also carved from a single rock.

56
00:02:41,732 --> 00:02:44,055
So here are the five
things not to miss:

57
00:02:44,637 --> 00:02:45,698
the hanging pillar,

58
00:02:46,079 --> 00:02:47,280
the ceiling paintings,

59
00:02:47,741 --> 00:02:52,668
the unfinished mandapa, the
Nagalinga, and the giant Nandi. Now,

60
00:02:53,029 --> 00:02:54,050
how do you get there?

61
00:02:54,551 --> 00:02:57,533
About one hundred and twenty-five
kilometres from Bengaluru,

62
00:02:57,553 --> 00:02:59,134
two and a half to three hours.

63
00:02:59,455 --> 00:03:01,336
Take a cab or bus to Hindupur.

64
00:03:01,356 --> 00:03:04,898
From there the temple is twelve
to fifteen kilometres away.

65
00:03:05,379 --> 00:03:08,201
By train, get off at Hindupur station,

66
00:03:08,621 --> 00:03:12,784
then take a taxi or auto. A cab
costs roughly thirty-three hundred to

67
00:03:12,804 --> 00:03:15,066
thirty-eight hundred rupees, one way.

68
00:03:16,107 --> 00:03:20,671
The bus is the cheapest. A Karnataka
State Road Transport Corporation bus,

69
00:03:21,051 --> 00:03:24,414
or an Andhra Pradesh State
Road Transport Corporation bus.

70
00:03:24,894 --> 00:03:27,677
Check the fare on their apps.
For darshan at the temple,

71
00:03:27,697 --> 00:03:30,539
there is either no ticket,
or a very small one.

72
00:03:31,667 --> 00:03:35,568
The temple usually opens from six in
the morning until six in the evening.

73
00:03:36,268 --> 00:03:38,509
October to March is the best time.

74
00:03:39,369 --> 00:03:41,270
Summers are hot and sunny,

75
00:03:41,650 --> 00:03:43,250
so go early in the morning,

76
00:03:43,591 --> 00:03:45,591
or in the evening. My plan.

77
00:03:45,991 --> 00:03:48,612
Leave Bengaluru at six in the morning,

78
00:03:48,912 --> 00:03:51,653
and reach the temple by
nine. First the pillar,

79
00:03:52,113 --> 00:03:53,193
then the ceiling,

80
00:03:53,574 --> 00:03:56,674
then the mandapa, then the Nagalinga,

81
00:03:56,975 --> 00:03:58,555
and finally the Nandi.

82
00:04:00,523 --> 00:04:03,184
Two to three hours is plenty,

83
00:04:03,584 --> 00:04:06,445
and be back by afternoon. Carry water,

84
00:04:06,865 --> 00:04:09,486
and comfortable sandals for walking.

85
00:04:09,866 --> 00:04:13,687
If you want to stay, the
nearest hotels are in Hindupur.

86
00:04:13,707 --> 00:04:14,988
Wear clean clothes,

87
00:04:15,368 --> 00:04:20,350
take your footwear off outside the
temple, and leave leather items at home.

88
00:04:20,370 --> 00:04:24,251
Lepakshi is the place where
even stones tell stories.

89
00:04:24,811 --> 00:04:26,574
Do go, at least once.

90
00:04:27,136 --> 00:04:31,062
And yes, this pillar can hang
in the air without any support,

91
00:04:31,804 --> 00:04:33,146
but my channel cannot.

92
00:04:33,467 --> 00:04:36,171
So subscribe, and give
it a little support too.

93
00:04:38,015 --> 00:04:41,100
And next time, do try the
cloth under the pillar.

94
00:04:41,582 --> 00:04:42,844
If the cloth goes through,

95
00:04:43,124 --> 00:04:44,306
tell me in the comments.

96
00:04:44,727 --> 00:04:46,811
If the pillar falls, not my fault.
